cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Arrow-type semigroupoids / transitive relation digraphs
  refined by arrow count, complete to 10 objects
message: If you use this software or data, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  # VERIFY BEFORE PUBLISHING: name order taken from the author's own correspondence
  # ("Sultanbek Alikhan", signing as "Alikhan"). Correct if this is the wrong way round.
  - family-names: Sultanbek
    given-names: Alikhan
    # orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000   # add if one exists
keywords:
  - transitive relations
  - semigroupoids
  - enumeration
  - posets
  - Burnside lemma
  - canonical augmentation
  - OEIS
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/USERNAME/trd-arrow-refined   # set before publishing
abstract: >-
  Complete enumeration of arrow-type semigroupoids by objects and arrows for 1 to 10
  objects, equivalently transitive relation digraphs on n unlabelled points with no
  isolated point counted by number of related pairs. Computed via the Brinkmann-McKay
  structure theorem as a weighted Burnside count over unlabelled posets, rather than by
  searching semigroupoids. Extends Table 1 of arXiv:2509.00837, which is complete to 7
  objects and partial at 8. Includes two independent implementations, one of which
  streams posets by canonical augmentation and collapses automorphism groups to cycle
  partitions, and the OEIS b-file for the resulting triangle.
references:
  - type: article
    title: Computational Exploration of Finite Semigroupoids
    authors:
      - family-names: Egri-Nagy
        given-names: Attila
      - family-names: Nehaniv
        given-names: Chrystopher L.
    year: 2025
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.00837
    notes: Source of the arrow refinement and the motivation for this computation.
  - type: article
    title: Counting unlabelled topologies and transitive relations
    authors:
      - family-names: Brinkmann
        given-names: Gunnar
      - family-names: McKay
        given-names: Brendan D.
    journal: Journal of Integer Sequences
    volume: 8
    year: 2005
    notes: Article 05.2.1. Source of the structure theorem and of A091073 to 15 points.
